<title>EGYPT: Stia full-yr profits fall 66 percent.</title>
<headline>Stia full-yr profits fall 66 percent.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stia/Nasr Woollen and Selected Textiles made net attributable profits of 7.187 million pounds in the financial year 1995/6, 66 percent down on 21 million in the previous year, an official source at the Public Enterprise Ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The financial year ends on June 30.</p>
<p>The profits, which are not audited, are equivalent to 6.56 pounds for each of the 1.095 million shares. The shares are listed on the exchange but no price was available on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The state plans to sell the company to an anchor investor within the next year.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 POUNDS</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
